Priority: 3
Area: Canvas
Status: done
Depends on: split-main-into-shell-and-modes, add-save-load-project-files, add-svg-export-eligibility

Goal:
Add typed text rendering in Canvas Mode so the user can place and preserve text directly on the canvas.

Context:
Typed text was part of the original product direction and plan, but it has not been implemented yet. The user now explicitly wants to write text on the screen.

Expected changes:

- add a text tool or equivalent text-entry flow in Canvas Mode
- render text items on the canvas with selection compatibility
- persist text items through save/load and mode-switch state
- include text items in SVG export eligibility and output where supported

Acceptance criteria:

- The user can create visible text on the canvas with a keyboard-driven entry flow.
- Text items survive save/load and mode switches.
- Text items can be selected and moved like other canvas content.
- SVG export handles text items honestly when the export target is otherwise compatible.

Notes:

- Keep the first pass intentionally simple: plain text placement is enough.
- Rich text, rotation, advanced font management, and editing inspectors are out of scope for the initial slice.
